        fouling_rate: 2,
        base_misfire: 3,
        smoke_output: 1,
        two_handed: true,
        first_year_available: 1873,
        historical_note: "The 'Gun that Won the West.' Chambered in .44-40 Winchester centerfire, it offered a stronger iron frame than the brass-framed 1866 and was the first Winchester to use a caliber also available in a revolver. Over 720,000 produced. Its 1876 Centennial variant was a larger-frame model in .45-75.",
        sources: ["Henshaw, 1993", "Williamson, 1952"],
    ),
    (
