        two_handed: true,
        first_year_available: 1874,
        historical_note: "The premier long-range rifle of the frontier, used by buffalo hunters and marksmen. Its falling-block action, invented by Christian Sharps in 1848, was renowned for accuracy at extreme ranges. The .45-70 Government cartridge could drop a bison at 500 yards. A buffalo hunter could kill 100 bison in a day with a Sharps.",
        sources: ["Sellers, 1978", "Venturino, 1999"],
    ),
