        two_handed: true,
        first_year_available: 1700,
        historical_note: "A self-bow carved from ash, favored by Kiowa and Lakota hunters. Silent and deadly, it leaves no smoke and gives no position away. Cannot be used with called shots due to the instinctive archer's release. Arrows must be retrieved after combat. A well-made ash bow could drive an arrow clean through a buffalo's ribcage at forty paces.",
        sources: ["Hämäläinen, 2008", "Ewers, 1955"],
